---
// Tween IOP, "Why a tween IOP?" (2026-11-18, replaces the photo carousel). A 9-year-old and a 16-year-old need
// different groups, the three things that make the tween program its own, and the schedule from the copy.
import Icon from "../../Icon.astro";
---
<figure class="gx on-dark" aria-label="A 9-year-old with school anxiety doesn't need the same group as a 16-year-old. The tween IOP for kids 8 to 12 has age-matched groups, play- and skills-based activities, and parents as part of treatment from day one. Monday to Thursday at 1420 Main St, Glastonbury, for 8 to 12 weeks.">
  <div class="gx-ne">
    <div class="gx-box is-on"><strong>9</strong><span>years old, school anxiety</span><small>Tween IOP · ages 8–12</small></div>
    <span class="gx-ne-sign" aria-hidden="true">≠</span>
    <div class="gx-box"><strong>16</strong><span>years old</span><small><a class="inl" href="/programs/teen-iop/">Teen IOP</a></small></div>
  </div>
  <p class="gx-t">Its own program, built for kids</p>
  <ul class="gx-tiles is-3">
    <li><span class="gx-i i-b"><Icon name="users" class="h-5 w-5" /></span>Age-matched groups</li>
    <li><span class="gx-i i-g"><Icon name="sparkles" class="h-5 w-5" /></span>Play- &amp; skills-based activities</li>
    <li><span class="gx-i i-s"><Icon name="heart-even" class="h-5 w-5" /></span>Parents in treatment from day one</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="gx-strip"><Icon name="calendar" class="h-5 w-5" /><span><b>Mon–Thu · 8–12 weeks</b> · <a class="inl" href="/location/glastonbury-ct-3/">1420 Main St, Glastonbury</a></span></p>
  <figcaption class="gx-foot"><Icon name="check" class="h-4 w-4" />Early help, before struggles harden into patterns</figcaption>
</figure>
